THE EXTENSION OF A LIST

one link, from the newer code to the listed one: added
  in the unit: [old; newer]
two links, the middle code declared deleted, its older version in the table: added
  in the unit: [old; newest]
    a chain from middle: reaches the list
the same with no table: the middle link is missing, not added
  in the unit: [old]
    a chain from newest: not known
the listed code id has no metadata anywhere: the link to it is enough
  in the unit: [old; newer]
the newer code listed: the older is not added
  in the unit: [newer]
    a chain from old: does not reach the list
two versions of one code, one listed: the other is not added
  in the unit: [left]
    a chain from root: does not reach the list
    a chain from right: does not reach the list
a cycle that has no listed code id: nothing added
  in the unit: [old]
    a chain from round: does not reach the list
    a chain from about: does not reach the list
a cycle one of whose code ids is listed: the other is added
  in the unit: [about; round]
one chain known, one with a missing link: one added
  in the unit: [old; newer]
    a chain from newest: not known
a call in the code of the prefix, a newer version bound by the unit: not added
  in the prefix: [old]
    a chain from far: reaches the list
    a chain from wrapper: does not reach the list
a call in the code of the prefix, a newer version in the prefix: added
  in the prefix: [old; newer]
    a chain from wrapper: does not reach the list
a call with no list: left alone
  in the unit: no list
the empty list: stays empty
  in the unit: []
    a chain from old: does not reach the list
    a chain from newer: does not reach the list
the newer version bound by a group after the code that has the call: out of scope, not added
  in the unit: [old]
    a chain from wrapper: does not reach the list
    a chain from newer: reaches the list
the newer version bound by the body of a Let_cont, the call in its handler: in scope, added
  in the unit: [old; newer]
three listed, one of them twice, and one added: in one order on the numbers of the model, none twice
  in the unit: [old; root; newer; left]

A RUN THAT STOPS AT A CALL OF KNOWN ARITY

the code of the callee is listed
  not undefined
the code of the callee is a newer version of the listed code and is not in the list
  undefined, and the unit is not checked: newer is a newer version of listed code that the list has not (the conversion adds such code only where it is in scope at the call)
the code of the callee has an older version of which nothing is known
  undefined, and the unit is not checked: newest may be a newer version of listed code: the metadata of one of its older versions are not at hand
the same, the table has the older version
  undefined, and the unit is not checked: newest is a newer version of listed code that the list has not (the conversion adds such code only where it is in scope at the call)
the code of the callee is known to be no version of the listed code
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
the empty list, whatever is known of the code of the callee
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
a newer version that is not in the list, and two arguments for code of one parameter
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
the callee is a number
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
the run stops at something that is not a call
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
a call with no list, of the newer version
  not undefined
a newer version that is not in the list, and an argument that has no value
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
a newer version that is not in the list, and a result of another arity than the code returns
  undefined, and reported as of any unit
code of the prefix calls its parameter with a list; the unit gives it a closure of a newer version that the unit binds (the lists extended first)
  undefined, and the unit is not checked: far is a newer version of listed code that the list has not (the conversion adds such code only where it is in scope at the call)
the same, the unit gives it a closure of the listed code
  not undefined
the same, the newer version is code of the prefix: it is in the list once extended
  not undefined
